WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:10.230
In education accountability era things
that don't boost math and reading scores

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:14.730
have fallen out of favor that includes
field trips but is this really much of a

00:00:14.730 --> 00:00:20.070
loss after all most of us can recall a
field trip that seemed more like a lark

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:24.689
than a learning experience that's what
makes the pioneering research by my

00:00:24.689 --> 00:00:29.340
friend University of Arkansas professor
Jay Greene so compelling using a gold

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:34.380
standard random assignment methodology
Greene has studied the impact of museum

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:39.000
visits and trips to the theater to see a
Shakespearean play he found that these

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:44.610
field trips had a significant impact on
knowledge retention remarkably he also

00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:49.050
found that such trips
similarly boosted students tolerance and

00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:54.930
empathy why green suggests that these
experiences help students register

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:59.070
things in ways that they don't in a
classroom setting Greene's work is a

00:00:59.070 --> 00:01:04.379
valuable argument that experiences which
have been pushed aside in our test

00:01:04.379 --> 00:01:10.560
obsessed era may deserve a second look
what do you think about field trips let

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:14.939
us know in your comments also let us
know what other topics you'd like our

00:01:14.939 --> 00:01:19.710
scholars to cover in 60 seconds and be
sure to LIKE and subscribe for more

00:01:19.710 --> 00:01:23.630
research and videos from AEI

